+--------------------------+                         +--------------------------+
Protocol Modes & Operational Rules
•	LACP Negotiation: Configured using active mode on both ends (channel-group 1 mode active), ensuring active LACP packet exchange. (The bank avoided passive + passive combinations, which fail to establish a link).

•	Configuration Consistency: All physical member interfaces were set to identical speeds, duplex modes, switchport trunking modes, native VLANs, and allowed VLAN lists before bundling into port-channel 1.

•	Traffic Load Balancing: Traffic across the bundled physical links is distributed per-flow using a source/destination IP and port frame header hash, guaranteeing that packet ordering within a single session is strictly maintained without exceeding individual member link speeds.

Section 4: Loop Prevention via Rapid PVST+ and STP Protections
To maintain physical hardware redundancy while eliminating switching loops, broadcast storms, and MAC table instability, Pubali Bank PLC deployed Rapid Per-VLAN Spanning Tree Plus (Rapid PVST+ / IEEE 802.1w).
