## 6. Cisco wireless architectures and AP modes

Architectures:

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Architecture  | How it works                                 | Analogy                                 |
|---------------|----------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------|
| Autonomous AP | Each AP is configured and managed on its own | A franchise shop setting its own policy |
| Cloud-based (Meraki) | AP managed from a cloud dashboard; user data stays local | Shops following policy pushed from a web HQ |
| Split-MAC (lightweight AP + WLC) | AP handles real-time work (RF, beacons, frame transmission, encryption); WLC handles management (authentication, roaming, RF management, security policy, QoS) | Cashier handles customers; head office approves policy |
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

CAPWAP tunnels: UDP 5246 (control) and UDP 5247 (data) between lightweight AP and WLC.

WLC deployments:
- Unified: a dedicated on-prem controller.
- Embedded: WLC runs on a Catalyst switch.
- Cloud-based: WLC hosted in cloud or private cloud.
- Mobility Express: WLC runs on an AP, for small sites.

AP modes:

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Mode        | Function |
|-------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Local       | Default. Serves clients and scans channels; CAPWAP to WLC                 |
| FlexConnect | Switches client traffic locally at the branch, even if the WLC link fails |
| Monitor     | Doesn't serve clients; scans for attacks and rogues                       |
| Rogue Detector | Listens on the wired side for rogue MAC addresses                      |
| Sniffer     | Captures packets and forwards them to an analyzer                         |
| Bridge/Mesh | Links buildings, point-to-point or point-to-multipoint                    |
| SE-Connect  | Acts as a spectrum analyzer                                               |
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

