## 7. WLC and AP management access

Methods:
- Console (physical)
- Telnet and HTTP (insecure)
- SSH and HTTPS (secure)
- SNMP
- Cloud dashboard (Meraki)

Authentication for admins: local users, RADIUS or TACACS+.

---------------------------------------------------------------------
|           | RADIUS        | TACACS+                                |
|-----------|---------------|----------------------------------------|
| Transport | UDP 1812/1813 | TCP 49                                 |
| Encrypts  | Password only | Entire payload                         |
| AAA       | Authentication and authorization combined | Separated  |
| Best for  | Network access (users, 802.1X) | Device administration |
---------------------------------------------------------------------

Physical connections:
- AP → switch access port in Local mode, in the AP management VLAN.
- FlexConnect AP → trunk port, because it switches multiple VLANs locally.
- WLC → switch trunk port, carrying all client VLANs.
- LAG bundles WLC ports. An AireOS WLC needs the switch side set to EtherChannel mode `on`, with no LACP or PAgP.

